 @Brave_New_Tube  First off. Your comment there would make a lot more sense if you hadn't ChatGPT'ed a response, i can't even attempt to comprehend what you're trying to convey.
And second. I literally gave you the dates, showing that you're wrong. You have no evidence.
Stop being a Netflix glazer.

 @Brave_New_Tube  It's the same team. And the economy clearly hasn't changed sufficiently to make jojo unprofitable.
The concept of streaming wasn't suddenly invented after 2019.
Again, weekly is faster, get over yourself.

 @BenisMannn  "Show me evidence that disproves my already-baseless assumptions that literally everything is the same and nothing is different between the production logistics of anime 5-10+ years ago and now" lol

And you're naive if you think the ramifications of COVID (or more specifically the world's overreaction to it) don't have lingering collateral effects still being experienced today.

And the vast vast majority of anime that are releasing weekly are also just seasonal batches with longer breaks in-between seasons. Very few still do serialized weekly uninterrupted on-air releases, and even those have occasional breaks.

 @Brave_New_Tube  A bunch of anime air weekly on Netflix (There goes your entire "argument")
38 weeks is shorter than a year.
Why are you still trying.
